   "topic": "Construction",
   "page": 1,
   "text": "An infrared LED on a GaAs chip and an NPN phototransistor on a silicon chip are mounted next to each other in one plastic body, both looking out of the same face. The part senses an object close in front of it by the LED light it reflects back into the transistor. The package cuts off visible wavelengths."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Light current and bins",
   "page": 3,
   "text": "Light current is the collector current with 20 mA in the LED and 5 V from collector to emitter. Parts are sorted by it into bin B (300 µA to 600 µA) and bin C (500 µA to 800 µA). Leakage current, with the same LED drive and bias, is 1 µA at most."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Derating",
   "page": 4,
   "text": "LED forward current is allowed to 50 mA up to 25 °C ambient and falls along a straight line to about 10 mA at 85 °C. Collector power dissipation is allowed to 75 mW up to 25 °C and falls along a straight line to about 12.6 mW at 85 °C."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Soldering",
   "page": 6,
   "text": "Reflow follows the Pb-free profile, two passes at most. No stress is to be put on the part while it is being heated, and the circuit board is not to be warped once soldered. Repair of a soldered part is to be avoided; when it is necessary, it is done with a double-head soldering iron, after confirming that repair will not damage the part's characteristics."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Moisture",
